## Quick Reference: Lesson 005

### DJNZ Instruction

| Instruction | Operation | T-states | Range |
|-------------|-----------|----------|-------|
| DJNZ label | B←B-1, if B≠0 jump | 13 (loop) / 8 (exit) | -126 to +129 bytes |

**Flags:** None affected

### Loop Patterns

**Counted loop:**
```asm
LD B,count
Loop:
    ; Code
    DJNZ Loop
```

**Loop with preserved position:**
```asm
LD B,count
Loop:
    PUSH DE          ; Save position
    ; Code that modifies DE
    POP DE           ; Restore position
    DJNZ Loop
```

**Nested loops:**
```asm
LD B,outer_count
OuterLoop:
    PUSH BC          ; Save outer counter
    LD B,inner_count
InnerLoop:
        ; Inner code
        DJNZ InnerLoop
    POP BC           ; Restore outer counter
    DJNZ OuterLoop
```

### Screen Addressing (Row 0)

| Scanline | Address (col 10) | Pattern |
|----------|------------------|---------|
| 0 | $400A | Base + column |
| 1 | $410A | Base + $100 + column |
| 2 | $420A | Base + $200 + column |
| 3 | $430A | Base + $300 + column |
| 4 | $440A | Base + $400 + column |
| 5 | $450A | Base + $500 + column |
| 6 | $460A | Base + $600 + column |
| 7 | $470A | Base + $700 + column |

**Navigation:** INC D moves to next scanline (+256 bytes)

### Performance Comparison

| Operation | Assembly (DJNZ) | BASIC | Advantage |
|-----------|-----------------|-------|-----------|
| Draw 5 blocks | ~650 T-states | ~25000 T-states | ~38× faster |
| Display "SNAKE" | ~1750 T-states | ~50000 T-states | ~28× faster |
| Draw 100 pixels | ~8000 T-states | ~500000 T-states | ~62× faster |

